  LegalTerm(term: 'Defendant', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The person against whom a civil suit or criminal case is filed.', usage: 'The defendant denied all allegations and filed a counter-claim for damages.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Petitioner', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The person who files a petition, typically in writ proceedings or family matters.', usage: 'The petitioner challenged the detention order under Article 226 of the Constitution.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Respondent', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The party against whom a petition or appeal is filed.', usage: 'The respondent filed counter-affidavit opposing the grant of bail.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Appellant', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The party who appeals a lower court decision to a higher court.', usage: 'The appellant challenged the conviction on grounds of insufficient evidence.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Complainant', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The person who lodges a criminal complaint or FIR.', usage: 'The complainant narrated the incident before the Magistrate under Section 223 BNSS.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Accused', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The person charged with a criminal offence.', usage: 'The accused was produced before the Magistrate within 24 hours of arrest.', section: 'Article 22 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Prosecution', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The legal party responsible for presenting the case against the accused in a criminal trial.', usage: 'The prosecution examined 15 witnesses during the trial to prove the charge of murder.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Defence', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The case presented by or on behalf of the accused to rebut the prosecution\'s case.', usage: 'The defence argued the accused was a minor at the time of the offence and should be tried as a juvenile.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Precedent', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A previous court decision that serves as a guide for deciding similar cases in the future.', usage: 'The Supreme Court judgment in Kesavananda Bharati is a binding precedent on the basic structure doctrine.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Jurisprudence', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The theory and philosophy of law; the study of the principles on which legal rules are based.', usage: 'Austin\'s jurisprudence defines law as the command of the sovereign backed by sanctions.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Deposition', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'Testimony of a witness given under oath, recorded in writing.', usage: 'The deposition of the eyewitness was crucial in establishing the guilt of the accused.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Subpoena', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A court order requiring a person to attend court to give evidence or produce documents.', usage: 'A subpoena was issued to the bank manager to produce the accused\'s bank statements.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Adjudication', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The formal judgment or decision by a court on a disputed matter.', usage: 'The adjudication of the property dispute took three years in the trial court.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Abatement', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The suspension or termination of legal proceedings, often due to the death of a party.', usage: 'The suit abated upon the death of the sole plaintiff as no legal heir was substituted within the prescribed time.', section: 'Order 22 CPC'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Abetment', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'Instigating, conspiring, or intentionally aiding another person to commit an offence.', usage: 'The accused was charged with abetment of suicide for continuously harassing the victim.', section: 'BNS Sec 45-48'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Absconding', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'Fleeing or hiding to avoid legal process or arrest.', usage: 'Non-bailable warrant was issued as the accused was absconding and evading service of summons.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Set Off', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A defendant\'s claim against the plaintiff for a sum not exceeding the plaintiff\'s claim. Used as a defence.', usage: 'The defendant claimed set off of ₹2,00,000 owed by the plaintiff under a separate transaction.', section: 'Order 8 Rule 6 CPC'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Counter Claim', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A claim made by the defendant against the plaintiff in the same suit.', usage: 'The defendant filed a counter claim for ₹5,00,000 as damages for defamation by the plaintiff.', section: 'Order 8 Rule 6A CPC'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Interpleader Suit', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A suit filed by a person against two or more claimants to the same property, asking the court to decide.', usage: 'The tenant filed an interpleader suit as both parties claimed to be the landlord.', section: 'Sec 88 CPC / Order 35 CPC'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Res Sub Judice', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A matter pending trial. No court shall try a suit in which the matter is already being tried in another court.', usage: 'The second suit was stayed under Section 10 CPC as the identical issue was res sub judice.', section: 'Sec 10 CPC'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Decree Holder', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The person in whose favour a decree has been passed.', usage: 'The decree holder filed an execution petition to recover the amount from the judgment debtor.', section: 'Sec 2(3) CPC'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Judgment Debtor', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The party against whom a decree for payment of money has been passed.', usage: 'The judgment debtor\'s property was attached for non-payment of the decretal amount.', section: 'Sec 2(10) CPC'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Execution', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The process of enforcing or giving effect to a court decree or order.', usage: 'An execution petition was filed to attach and sell the immovable property of the judgment debtor.', section: 'Sec 36-74 CPC'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Vakalatnama', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A document authorizing an advocate to appear and act on behalf of a party in court.', usage: 'The advocate filed his vakalatnama before making any submission on behalf of the client.'),

  // ═══ CRIMINAL LAW ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Cognizable Offence', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'An offence in which police can arrest without warrant and investigate without court permission.', usage: 'Murder is a cognizable offence — police must register FIR and may arrest without a warrant.', section: 'Sec 2(1)(c) BNSS'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Non-Cognizable Offence', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'An offence in which police cannot arrest without warrant and cannot investigate without court permission.', usage: 'Simple assault is a non-cognizable offence. A private complaint must be filed before the Magistrate.', section: 'Sec 2(1)(l) BNSS'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Bailable Offence', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'An offence where the accused has a right to be released on bail.', usage: 'Cheating is a bailable offence; the accused is entitled to bail as of right.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Compounding', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Settlement of a criminal case between the complainant and accused with court permission.', usage: 'The complainant agreed to compound the case of hurt under BNS Sec 115(2) upon receiving compensation.', section: 'Sec 359 BNSS'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Bail Bond', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'A written undertaking by the accused (with sureties) to appear before court and comply with conditions.', usage: 'The accused executed a bail bond of ₹1,00,000 with two local sureties.', section: 'Sec 478 BNSS'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Murder', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'The unlawful killing of a human being with the intention to cause death or bodily injury likely to cause death.', usage: 'The accused was charged with murder under BNS Sec 103(1) for stabbing the victim with a knife.', section: 'BNS Sec 101-103'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Culpable Homicide', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Causing death by an act done with the intention or knowledge that it is likely to cause death, but without the degree of intention required for murder.', usage: 'The death resulted from a rash act without premeditation — charged as culpable homicide not amounting to murder.', section: 'BNS Sec 100'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Grievous Hurt', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Injuries that endanger life or cause severe pain, permanent disability, or disfigurement.', usage: 'The victim suffered a fracture of the skull, classified as grievous hurt.', section: 'BNS Sec 117'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Criminal Misappropriation', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Dishonestly converting to one\'s own use property that comes into possession lawfully.', usage: 'The accountant was charged with criminal misappropriation for diverting company funds to his personal account.', section: 'BNS Sec 316'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Criminal Breach of Trust', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Dishonestly misappropriating or converting property entrusted to oneself.', usage: 'The trustee sold charity property and pocketed the proceeds — charged with criminal breach of trust.', section: 'BNS Sec 316'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Cheating', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Deceiving a person to fraudulently induce them to deliver property or alter a valuable security.', usage: 'The accused cheated the victim by impersonating a bank officer and obtaining ₹5,00,000.', section: 'BNS Sec 318'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Forgery', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Making a false document with the intent to deceive or cause damage.', usage: 'The accused committed forgery by fabricating a sale deed with a forged signature.', section: 'BNS Sec 336'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Dacoity', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Robbery committed by five or more persons acting together.', usage: 'Five armed men broke into the house and looted valuables — charged with dacoity.', section: 'BNS Sec 310'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Robbery', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Theft or extortion accompanied by violence or fear of violence.', usage: 'The accused snatched the gold chain from the victim after threatening her with a knife — charged with robbery.', section: 'BNS Sec 309'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Extortion', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Obtaining property or valuable security through coercion, threats, or intimidation.', usage: 'The accused sent threatening messages demanding ₹10,00,000 — charged with extortion.', section: 'BNS Sec 308'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Kidnapping', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Taking or enticing a minor or person of unsound mind out of the keeping of their lawful guardian.', usage: 'The accused kidnapped the 10-year-old child from the school premises.', section: 'BNS Sec 137'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Abduction', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Compelling or inducing a person to go from one place to another by force or deceit.', usage: 'The girl was abducted by force and taken to another state.', section: 'BNS Sec 137'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Defamation', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Making or publishing false statements that harm the reputation of another person.', usage: 'The newspaper article containing false allegations constituted criminal defamation.', section: 'BNS Sec 356'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Sedition', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Acts or words intended to incite disaffection, contempt, or hatred against the government.', usage: 'The speech was alleged to be seditious for calling for the violent overthrow of the elected government.', section: 'BNS Sec 152'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Dowry Death', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Death of a woman within 7 years of marriage under suspicious circumstances related to dowry demands.', usage: 'The in-laws were charged with dowry death as the bride died within 2 years of marriage due to burn injuries.', section: 'BNS Sec 80'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Cruelty', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Willful conduct likely to drive a woman to commit suicide or cause grave injury or danger to her life, limb, or health.', usage: 'The wife filed a complaint of cruelty alleging persistent dowry demands and physical abuse by the husband and in-laws.', section: 'BNS Sec 85'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Mischief', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Intentionally destroying or damaging property, or diminishing its value or utility.', usage: 'The accused was charged with mischief for setting fire to the crops in the field.', section: 'BNS Sec 324'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Criminal Trespass', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Entering upon the property of another with intent to commit an offence, annoy, or intimidate.', usage: 'The accused broke into the locked house at night — charged with criminal trespass.', section: 'BNS Sec 329'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'House Breaking', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Entering a building used as a human dwelling by making an entry through a passage not intended for that purpose.', usage: 'The accused entered through the window at night — charged with house breaking.', section: 'BNS Sec 331'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Assault', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'An act that causes reasonable apprehension of the use of criminal force.', usage: 'Raising a fist and advancing towards the victim amounts to assault even without physical contact.', section: 'BNS Sec 130'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Rioting', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Use of force or violence by an unlawful assembly (five or more persons) in pursuit of a common object.', usage: 'The mob attacked the shops — all members were charged with rioting.', section: 'BNS Sec 189'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Attempt', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'An act done with the intent to commit a crime that goes beyond mere preparation but falls short of completion.', usage: 'The accused was charged with attempted murder as the gunshot missed the victim narrowly.', section: 'BNS Sec 109'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Conspiracy', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'An agreement between two or more persons to do an illegal act or a legal act by illegal means.', usage: 'All three accused conspired to defraud the bank of ₹50 crore — charged with criminal conspiracy.', section: 'BNS Sec 61'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Parole', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Temporary release of a prisoner before the completion of the sentence, on conditions.', usage: 'The convict was granted 30 days parole on compassionate grounds to attend his mother\'s funeral.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Probation', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Release of a convicted person under supervision instead of imprisonment, usually for first-time offenders.', usage: 'The first-time offender was released on probation for one year under the Probation of Offenders Act.', section: 'Probation of Offenders Act, 1958'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Commutation', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Reduction of a sentence to a less severe one, usually by the executive authority.', usage: 'The death sentence was commuted to life imprisonment by the Governor under Article 161.', section: 'Article 72, 161 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Confession', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'A voluntary statement by the accused admitting guilt. Must be made before a Magistrate to be admissible.', usage: 'The confession recorded by the Magistrate under Section 183 BNSS was the key evidence in the case.', section: 'Sec 183 BNSS / Sec 24-26 BSA'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Approver', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'An accomplice in a crime who turns witness for the prosecution in exchange for a pardon.', usage: 'The co-accused became an approver and testified against the main accused in exchange for pardon.', section: 'Sec 343 BNSS'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Inquest', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'A preliminary investigation into the cause of an unnatural death, conducted by police or Magistrate.', usage: 'The police conducted an inquest at the scene to determine the cause of death.', section: 'Sec 194 BNSS'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Panchnama', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'An official record prepared by police in the presence of independent witnesses (panchas) during investigation.', usage: 'The seizure panchnama recorded the recovery of the weapon from the accused\'s residence.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Charge', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'A formal accusation of a specific offence framed by the court against the accused.', usage: 'The court framed charges under BNS Section 103(1) and Section 61 after hearing arguments.', section: 'Sec 230 BNSS'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Discharge', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Release of the accused by the court when no sufficient grounds exist for proceeding with the trial.', usage: 'The accused was discharged under Section 227 BNSS as the prosecution failed to make out a prima facie case.', section: 'Sec 227 BNSS'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Plea Bargaining', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'A pre-trial negotiation where the accused pleads guilty to a lesser charge in exchange for a lighter sentence.', usage: 'The accused opted for plea bargaining and received a reduced sentence of community service.', section: 'Sec 290-294 BNSS'),

  // ═══ EVIDENCE ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Dying Declaration', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'A statement made by a person who is about to die, regarding the cause or circumstances of their death.', usage: 'The dying declaration recorded by the Magistrate was the sole basis of conviction.', section: 'Sec 26 BSA (Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam)'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Hearsay', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'Evidence based on what a witness heard from someone else, not from personal knowledge. Generally inadmissible.', usage: 'The testimony was rejected as hearsay since the witness did not personally see the incident.', section: 'BSA General Principles'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Circumstantial Evidence', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'Evidence that relies on inference to connect facts to a conclusion, rather than direct testimony.', usage: 'The chain of circumstantial evidence was complete, pointing only to the guilt of the accused.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Corroboration', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'Supporting evidence that confirms or strengthens existing testimony.', usage: 'The approver\'s testimony requires corroboration on material particulars before conviction.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Cross-Examination', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'Questioning of a witness by the opposing party to test credibility and accuracy.', usage: 'During cross-examination, the prosecution witness contradicted his own statement.', section: 'Sec 145 BSA'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Examination-in-Chief', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'Questioning of a witness by the party who called them.', usage: 'In examination-in-chief, the plaintiff narrated the entire transaction leading to the dispute.', section: 'Sec 143 BSA'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Re-examination', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'Further questioning by the party who called the witness, after cross-examination, to clarify points.', usage: 'In re-examination, the witness clarified the discrepancy raised during cross-examination.', section: 'Sec 146 BSA'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Burden of Proof', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'The obligation to prove a disputed fact. In civil cases on the plaintiff, in criminal on prosecution.', usage: 'The burden of proof lies on the prosecution to prove guilt beyond reasonable doubt.', section: 'Sec 104 BSA'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Beyond Reasonable Doubt', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'The standard of proof in criminal cases — the evidence must be so convincing that no reasonable doubt remains.', usage: 'The prosecution failed to prove the charge beyond reasonable doubt, resulting in acquittal.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Preponderance of Probability', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'The standard of proof in civil cases — more likely than not.', usage: 'On preponderance of probability, the court found the plaintiff\'s version more credible.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Admissibility', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'Whether evidence can be legally presented in court based on rules of evidence.', usage: 'The electronic evidence was held inadmissible as it lacked the certificate required under Section 63 BSA.', section: 'Sec 63 BSA'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Relevancy', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'The logical connection between a fact and the matter in issue. Only relevant facts are admissible.', usage: 'The evidence of the accused\'s character was held relevant to show motive for the crime.', section: 'Sec 5 BSA'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Primary Evidence', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'The original document itself produced for inspection of the court.', usage: 'The original sale deed was produced as primary evidence of the transaction.', section: 'Sec 57 BSA'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Secondary Evidence', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'Copies, certified copies, or oral accounts of document contents when the original is unavailable.', usage: 'A certified copy of the FIR was admitted as secondary evidence since the original was lost.', section: 'Sec 58 BSA'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Electronic Evidence', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'Information stored or transmitted in electronic form, including emails, CCTV footage, and digital documents.', usage: 'WhatsApp messages were admitted as electronic evidence with proper Section 63 BSA certification.', section: 'Sec 63 BSA'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Expert Witness', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'A witness with specialized knowledge in a field who gives opinion evidence to assist the court.', usage: 'A forensic expert testified that the handwriting on the forged document matched the accused\'s writing.', section: 'Sec 39 BSA'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Hostile Witness', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'A witness who turns against the party that called them and gives adverse testimony.', usage: 'The prosecution witness turned hostile in court and contradicted his police statement.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Presumption', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'A legal inference that a court draws from established facts, until disproved.', usage: 'There is a presumption of innocence — every accused is presumed innocent until proven guilty.', section: 'Sec 118 BSA'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Judicial Notice', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'Facts that the court accepts as true without formal proof, as they are common knowledge.', usage: 'The court took judicial notice of the fact that Diwali is a national holiday in India.', section: 'Sec 56-57 BSA'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Res Gestae', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'Things done or statements made as part of the transaction itself, so closely connected that they form part of it.', usage: 'The victim\'s cry for help immediately after the attack was admissible as res gestae.', section: 'Sec 4 BSA'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Test Identification Parade', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'A procedure where a witness identifies the accused among similar-looking persons to confirm identity.', usage: 'The accused was identified by the victim in the TIP conducted by the Magistrate.', section: 'Sec 8 BSA'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Documentary Evidence', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'Evidence in the form of documents, including written records, electronic records, and photographs.', usage: 'The registered sale deed was produced as documentary evidence to prove ownership.', section: 'Sec 57-63 BSA'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Oral Evidence', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'Testimony given by witnesses in court through spoken words.', usage: 'The eyewitness gave oral evidence describing the sequence of events at the crime scene.', section: 'Sec 56 BSA'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Opinion Evidence', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'Evidence given by experts based on their specialized knowledge. Generally, witnesses of fact cannot give opinions.', usage: 'The DNA expert\'s opinion evidence established that the blood found at the crime scene matched the accused.', section: 'Sec 39-44 BSA'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Character Evidence', category: 'Evidence', meaning: 'Evidence about a person\'s general reputation or disposition. Limited admissibility in criminal cases.', usage: 'In criminal cases, the accused may prove good character to negate the presumption of guilt.', section: 'Sec 52-55 BSA'),

  // ═══ PROPERTY LAW ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Lien', category: 'Property', meaning: 'The right to retain possession of another\'s property until a debt owed by the owner is discharged.', usage: 'The banker exercised his general lien over the securities deposited by the customer.', section: 'Sec 170-171 Indian Contract Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Mortgage', category: 'Property', meaning: 'Transfer of an interest in immovable property as security for a loan.', usage: 'The borrower created an equitable mortgage by depositing title deeds with the bank.', section: 'Sec 58 Transfer of Property Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Easement', category: 'Property', meaning: 'A right to use another person\'s land for a specific purpose (e.g., right of way).', usage: 'The plaintiff claimed easementary right of way over the defendant\'s property by long usage.', section: 'Indian Easements Act, 1882'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Encumbrance', category: 'Property', meaning: 'A claim or liability attached to property, such as a mortgage or lien.', usage: 'The EC (Encumbrance Certificate) showed no encumbrance on the property for the last 30 years.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Title', category: 'Property', meaning: 'Legal ownership rights over property.', usage: 'The plaintiff proved his title by producing the registered sale deed and revenue records.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Partition', category: 'Property', meaning: 'Division of jointly owned property among co-owners.', usage: 'A suit for partition was filed seeking division of ancestral property among all legal heirs.', section: 'Sec 4 Partition Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Adverse Possession', category: 'Property', meaning: 'Acquiring ownership rights over property by continuous, open, and hostile possession for the statutory period.', usage: 'The plaintiff claimed title by adverse possession after 12 years of uninterrupted, hostile possession.', section: 'Article 65 Limitation Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Mesne Profits', category: 'Property', meaning: 'Profits which a wrongful occupant has earned from property. Payable to the rightful owner.', usage: 'The court directed the defendant to pay mesne profits at ₹10,000/month for the period of wrongful occupation.', section: 'Sec 2(12) CPC'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Coparcener', category: 'Property', meaning: 'A person who shares equally in inheritance of an undivided Hindu ancestral estate. Post-2005 amendment includes daughters.', usage: 'The daughter claimed her right as a coparcener in the joint Hindu family property.', section: 'Sec 6 Hindu Succession Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Karta', category: 'Property', meaning: 'The manager of a Hindu Undivided Family (HUF), usually the eldest male member.', usage: 'The Karta alienated ancestral property claiming legal necessity for the family.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Streedhan', category: 'Property', meaning: 'Property that belongs exclusively to a Hindu woman — gifts received before, during, or after marriage.', usage: 'The gold jewellery given at marriage is her streedhan and the husband has no right over it.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Sale Deed', category: 'Property', meaning: 'A registered document that transfers ownership of immovable property from the seller to the buyer.', usage: 'The sale deed was registered at the Sub-Registrar\'s office as required under Section 17 Registration Act.', section: 'Sec 54 Transfer of Property Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Gift Deed', category: 'Property', meaning: 'A document transferring property from one person to another without consideration, out of love and affection.', usage: 'The mother executed a registered gift deed in favour of her daughter.', section: 'Sec 122 Transfer of Property Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Lease', category: 'Property', meaning: 'A transfer of the right to enjoy immovable property for a specified period in return for rent.', usage: 'The lease was for a period of 11 months, renewable upon mutual consent.', section: 'Sec 105 Transfer of Property Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Tenancy', category: 'Property', meaning: 'The right to occupy land or property as a tenant under a lease agreement.', usage: 'The tenant claimed protection under the Rent Control Act against arbitrary eviction.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Eviction', category: 'Property', meaning: 'The lawful removal of a tenant from rented premises, typically through court proceedings.', usage: 'The landlord filed an eviction suit on grounds of non-payment of rent and bona fide personal need.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Possession', category: 'Property', meaning: 'Physical control or occupancy over property. Can be lawful or unlawful.', usage: 'The plaintiff proved prior exclusive possession through revenue records and electricity bills.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Encroachment', category: 'Property', meaning: 'Unauthorized occupation or extension onto another person\'s property or public land.', usage: 'The municipality issued a demolition notice for encroachment on government land.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Revenue Record', category: 'Property', meaning: 'Official land record maintained by the government showing ownership, area, and land use.', usage: 'The revenue records (khata/patta) confirmed the plaintiff\'s ownership of the agricultural land.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Mutation', category: 'Property', meaning: 'The process of updating revenue records to reflect a change in ownership of property.', usage: 'After the sale, mutation was applied for in the Revenue Office to update the land records in the buyer\'s name.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Will', category: 'Property', meaning: 'A legal document expressing a person\'s wishes for distribution of their property after death.', usage: 'The testator executed a will bequeathing the entire estate to his wife.', section: 'Indian Succession Act, 1925'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Probate', category: 'Property', meaning: 'Official certification by the court that a will is valid and authorizing the executor to administer the estate.', usage: 'Probate of the will was granted by the District Court, confirming its validity.', section: 'Sec 276 Indian Succession Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Succession', category: 'Property', meaning: 'The process by which property of a deceased person passes to their legal heirs.', usage: 'Intestate succession applied as the deceased died without leaving a will.', section: 'Hindu Succession Act / Indian Succession Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Intestate', category: 'Property', meaning: 'Dying without leaving a valid will. Property passes to heirs according to personal law.', usage: 'The deceased died intestate; the property devolved on Class I heirs under the Hindu Succession Act.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Testate', category: 'Property', meaning: 'Dying with a valid will in place.', usage: 'The deceased died testate, and the executor applied for probate to give effect to the will.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Usufructuary Mortgage', category: 'Property', meaning: 'A mortgage where the mortgagee takes possession and receives rents and profits in lieu of interest.', usage: 'A usufructuary mortgage was created where the lender took possession of the agricultural land and retained the crop income.', section: 'Sec 58(d) Transfer of Property Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Benami Property', category: 'Property', meaning: 'Property held in the name of one person but paid for by another, with the intention to conceal the real owner.', usage: 'The property was declared benami and confiscated by the government under the Benami Transactions Act.', section: 'Prohibition of Benami Property Transactions Act, 1988'),

  // ═══ CONSTITUTIONAL LAW ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Fundamental Rights', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'Basic rights guaranteed under Part III of the Constitution (Articles 12-35).', usage: 'The detention was challenged as violating the fundamental right to life under Article 21.', section: 'Part III Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'DPSP', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'Directive Principles of State Policy. Guidelines for the State in policy making, not enforceable by courts.', usage: 'DPSP under Article 39(b) directs the State to distribute material resources for the common good.', section: 'Part IV Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Preamble', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'The introductory statement of the Constitution setting out its guiding purpose and philosophy.', usage: 'The Preamble declares India to be a Sovereign, Socialist, Secular, Democratic Republic.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Basic Structure', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'The fundamental framework of the Constitution that cannot be altered or destroyed even by amendment.', usage: 'The Supreme Court in Kesavananda Bharati held that Parliament cannot amend the basic structure of the Constitution.', section: 'Kesavananda Bharati v. State of Kerala, 1973'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Judicial Review', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'The power of the judiciary to examine the constitutionality of legislative acts and executive actions.', usage: 'The High Court exercised judicial review to strike down the unconstitutional notification.', section: 'Article 13, 32, 226 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Separation of Powers', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'The constitutional principle that divides government into three branches: Legislature, Executive, and Judiciary.', usage: 'The court held that the executive order encroached upon legislative domain, violating separation of powers.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Federalism', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'The division of powers between the Union and State governments as listed in the Seventh Schedule.', usage: 'The state law was held ultra vires as the subject fell under the Union List in the Seventh Schedule.', section: 'Article 245-254 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Emergency', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'Extraordinary powers invoked by the President during war, internal disturbance, or financial crisis.', usage: 'During a national emergency, fundamental rights under Article 19 stand suspended.', section: 'Article 352-360 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'President\'s Rule', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'Imposition of direct Central government rule in a state when the state government cannot function per the Constitution.', usage: 'President\'s Rule was imposed in the state after the Governor reported Constitutional machinery had failed.', section: 'Article 356 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Ordinance', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'A law promulgated by the President or Governor when the legislature is not in session, having the force of an Act.', usage: 'The government promulgated an ordinance to ban the practice, which was later replaced by an Act of Parliament.', section: 'Article 123, 213 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Amendment', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'A formal change or addition to the Constitution, made by Parliament following the procedure under Article 368.', usage: 'The 42nd Amendment (1976) inserted the words "Socialist" and "Secular" into the Preamble.', section: 'Article 368 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Fundamental Duties', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'A list of moral obligations of citizens towards the nation, added by the 42nd Amendment in Part IVA.', usage: 'Article 51A lists fundamental duties including respect for the Constitution and the national flag.', section: 'Article 51A Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Right to Equality', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'The right guaranteed under Articles 14-18, prohibiting discrimination by the State on grounds of religion, race, caste, sex, or place of birth.', usage: 'The rule reserving government jobs only for men was struck down as violating the right to equality under Article 16.', section: 'Article 14-18 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Right to Freedom', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'Six freedoms guaranteed under Article 19, including speech, assembly, movement, residence, profession, and association.', usage: 'The ban on protests was challenged as a violation of the right to freedom of speech and assembly.', section: 'Article 19 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Right to Life', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'No person shall be deprived of life or personal liberty except according to procedure established by law.', usage: 'The Supreme Court expanded Article 21 to include the right to clean environment, privacy, and dignity.', section: 'Article 21 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Right to Education', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'Free and compulsory education for all children aged 6-14 years, added by the 86th Amendment.', usage: 'Under Article 21A, the State must provide free education to every child in the 6-14 age group.', section: 'Article 21A Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Right Against Exploitation', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'Prohibition of traffic in human beings, forced labour, and employment of children in hazardous occupations.', usage: 'Employing children below 14 in a factory violates Article 24 — right against exploitation.', section: 'Article 23-24 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Right to Privacy', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'The right to privacy is a fundamental right under Article 21, as held by the Supreme Court.', usage: 'In K.S. Puttaswamy (2017), the Supreme Court held that the right to privacy is intrinsic to Article 21.', section: 'Article 21 Constitution / Puttaswamy, 2017'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Reservation', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'The policy of reserving seats in education and government jobs for SC, ST, and OBC categories.', usage: 'The 50% cap on reservation was upheld in the Indra Sawhney case, with exceptions for extraordinary situations.', section: 'Article 15(4), 16(4) Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Governor', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'The constitutional head of a state, appointed by the President, acting on the aid and advice of the Council of Ministers.', usage: 'The Governor withheld assent to the state bill and reserved it for the President\'s consideration.', section: 'Article 153-167 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Speaker', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'The presiding officer of the Lok Sabha or State Legislative Assembly who maintains order and decides on procedure.', usage: 'The Speaker disqualified the MLA under the anti-defection law for voting against the party whip.', section: 'Article 93 / Tenth Schedule Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Anti-Defection Law', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'Law disqualifying elected members who defect from the party on whose ticket they were elected.', usage: 'The legislator was disqualified under the Tenth Schedule for voluntarily giving up party membership.', section: 'Tenth Schedule Constitution'),

  // ═══ FAMILY LAW ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Nikah', category: 'Family', meaning: 'Islamic marriage contract. A solemn agreement between bride and groom with witnesses and mahr.', usage: 'The validity of nikah was disputed as the bride\'s consent was allegedly not freely given.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Mahr', category: 'Family', meaning: 'Dower in Muslim law. The obligatory gift (money or property) given by the husband to the wife at marriage.', usage: 'The wife filed a suit for recovery of unpaid mahr of ₹5,00,000 agreed at the time of nikah.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Iddat', category: 'Family', meaning: 'The waiting period a Muslim woman must observe after divorce or death of husband before remarrying.', usage: 'The husband is liable to maintain the wife during the iddat period of three menstrual cycles.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Talaq', category: 'Family', meaning: 'Divorce in Muslim law. The dissolution of marriage by the husband pronouncing divorce.', usage: 'Triple talaq in one sitting was declared unconstitutional by the Supreme Court in Shayara Bano (2017).'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Khula', category: 'Family', meaning: 'Divorce initiated by the wife in Muslim law, usually with return of mahr to the husband.', usage: 'The wife obtained khula by mutual agreement, returning the mahr amount to the husband.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Wakf', category: 'Family', meaning: 'Permanent dedication of movable or immovable property by a Muslim for religious or charitable purposes.', usage: 'The property was registered as wakf and cannot be transferred as it is dedicated for public charity.', section: 'Wakf Act, 1995'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Maintenance', category: 'Family', meaning: 'Financial support that a person is legally obligated to provide to their spouse, children, or parents.', usage: 'The wife filed for maintenance under Section 144 BNSS claiming the husband earns ₹1,00,000 per month.', section: 'Sec 144 BNSS / Hindu Adoptions & Maintenance Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Alimony', category: 'Family', meaning: 'Financial provision ordered by the court for a spouse after divorce or separation.', usage: 'The court ordered permanent alimony of ₹25,000 per month to the wife upon granting mutual divorce.', section: 'Sec 25 Hindu Marriage Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Custody', category: 'Family', meaning: 'The rights and responsibilities of a parent for the care, control, and upbringing of a child.', usage: 'The mother was granted custody of the 5-year-old child, with visitation rights to the father.', section: 'Guardians and Wards Act, 1890'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Guardianship', category: 'Family', meaning: 'The legal authority to care for a minor\'s person or property.', usage: 'The maternal uncle was appointed guardian of the orphaned minor by the District Court.', section: 'Guardians and Wards Act, 1890'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Adoption', category: 'Family', meaning: 'The legal process of taking another\'s child as one\'s own, with the same rights as a biological child.', usage: 'The adoption was valid under Hindu law as both the adopting father and the child met the conditions under the Act.', section: 'Hindu Adoptions & Maintenance Act / JJ Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Divorce', category: 'Family', meaning: 'Legal dissolution of a marriage by a court decree, ending the marital relationship.', usage: 'The wife filed a petition for divorce on grounds of cruelty and desertion under Section 13 Hindu Marriage Act.', section: 'Sec 13 Hindu Marriage Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Mutual Consent Divorce', category: 'Family', meaning: 'Divorce granted when both spouses jointly petition the court, agreeing to dissolve the marriage.', usage: 'The parties filed for mutual consent divorce after settling issues of maintenance, custody, and property.', section: 'Sec 13B Hindu Marriage Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Restitution of Conjugal Rights', category: 'Family', meaning: 'A court decree directing a spouse who has withdrawn from cohabitation to return to the matrimonial home.', usage: 'The husband filed for restitution of conjugal rights after the wife left the matrimonial home without reason.', section: 'Sec 9 Hindu Marriage Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Judicial Separation', category: 'Family', meaning: 'A court decree allowing spouses to live apart without dissolving the marriage.', usage: 'Judicial separation was granted as the wife proved cruelty but did not seek divorce.', section: 'Sec 10 Hindu Marriage Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Domestic Violence', category: 'Family', meaning: 'Physical, emotional, verbal, sexual, or economic abuse against a woman in a domestic relationship.', usage: 'The wife obtained a protection order under the Domestic Violence Act restraining the husband from any contact.', section: 'Protection of Women from Domestic Violence Act, 2005'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Protection Order', category: 'Family', meaning: 'A court order protecting a person from domestic violence, restraining the abuser from certain acts.', usage: 'The Magistrate passed a protection order prohibiting the respondent from entering the shared household.', section: 'Sec 18 DV Act, 2005'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Dowry', category: 'Family', meaning: 'Property or valuable security given or agreed to be given by one party to a marriage to the other party.', usage: 'Demanding dowry is a criminal offence punishable under the Dowry Prohibition Act.', section: 'Dowry Prohibition Act, 1961'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Bigamy', category: 'Family', meaning: 'The offence of marrying a second time while the first marriage is still subsisting.', usage: 'The second marriage was void as the husband committed bigamy while his first wife was alive.', section: 'BNS Sec 82 / Sec 5 Hindu Marriage Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Void Marriage', category: 'Family', meaning: 'A marriage that is invalid from its inception and has no legal effect.', usage: 'The marriage was declared void as the husband had a living spouse at the time of the second marriage.', section: 'Sec 11 Hindu Marriage Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Voidable Marriage', category: 'Family', meaning: 'A marriage that is valid until annulled by a competent court at the option of the aggrieved party.', usage: 'The marriage was declared voidable as the consent was obtained by force — annulled by court decree.', section: 'Sec 12 Hindu Marriage Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Legitimacy', category: 'Family', meaning: 'The status of a child born within a valid marriage — a legitimate child has full inheritance rights.', usage: 'The child born within wedlock is presumed legitimate unless strong evidence proves otherwise.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Live-in Relationship', category: 'Family', meaning: 'A domestic arrangement where an unmarried couple lives together in a long-term relationship akin to marriage.', usage: 'The Supreme Court held that a woman in a long-term live-in relationship has the right to claim maintenance.'),

  // ═══ CONTRACT LAW ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Contract', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'An agreement enforceable by law, made with free consent, between competent parties, for lawful consideration and object.', usage: 'The agreement to sell the car for ₹5,00,000 constitutes a valid contract under the Indian Contract Act.', section: 'Sec 2(h) Indian Contract Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Offer', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'A proposal made by one person to another, expressing willingness to enter into a contract on certain terms.', usage: 'The seller\'s advertisement was held to be an invitation to offer, not an offer itself.', section: 'Sec 2(a) Indian Contract Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Acceptance', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'The unconditional assent to all terms of an offer, communicated to the offeror.', usage: 'The buyer\'s email confirming the purchase constituted valid acceptance of the seller\'s offer.', section: 'Sec 2(b) Indian Contract Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Consideration', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'Something of value given by each party to a contract. A contract without consideration is void.', usage: 'The promise to pay ₹10,000 for painting the house has adequate consideration — the painting work.', section: 'Sec 2(d) Indian Contract Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Free Consent', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'Consent not obtained by coercion, undue influence, fraud, misrepresentation, or mistake.', usage: 'The contract was voidable as consent was obtained by fraud — the seller misrepresented the age of the vehicle.', section: 'Sec 14 Indian Contract Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Void Agreement', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'An agreement not enforceable by law from the beginning — has no legal effect.', usage: 'An agreement in restraint of trade is void under Section 27 of the Indian Contract Act.', section: 'Sec 2(g) Indian Contract Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Voidable Contract', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'A contract that is valid but can be set aside at the option of the aggrieved party.', usage: 'The contract obtained by coercion is voidable at the option of the party whose consent was so caused.', section: 'Sec 2(i) Indian Contract Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Breach of Contract', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'Failure of a party to perform their obligations under the contract without lawful excuse.', usage: 'The supplier committed breach of contract by failing to deliver goods within the stipulated time.', section: 'Sec 73 Indian Contract Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Liquidated Damages', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'A predetermined amount agreed upon by parties as compensation payable in case of breach.', usage: 'The contract specified liquidated damages of ₹1,00,000 per week for delay in completion.', section: 'Sec 74 Indian Contract Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Guarantee', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'A promise to perform the obligation of another person in case of their default.', usage: 'The father stood as guarantor for his son\'s business loan of ₹50,00,000 from the bank.', section: 'Sec 126 Indian Contract Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Surety', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'A person who guarantees the performance of another person\'s obligation or the payment of their debt.', usage: 'The surety became liable when the principal debtor defaulted on the loan repayment.', section: 'Sec 126 Indian Contract Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Agency', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'A relationship where one person (agent) acts on behalf of another (principal) in dealings with third parties.', usage: 'The real estate agent was authorized by the principal to negotiate the sale of the property.', section: 'Sec 182 Indian Contract Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Power of Attorney', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'A written authority given by one person to another to act on their behalf in legal or financial matters.', usage: 'The NRI gave a general power of attorney to his brother to sell the ancestral property.', section: 'Powers of Attorney Act, 1882'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Force Majeure', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'An unforeseeable event beyond the control of parties that prevents performance of contractual obligations.', usage: 'The contractor invoked the force majeure clause after the pandemic made completion impossible.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Frustration', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'When a contract becomes impossible to perform due to an unforeseen event, it becomes void.', usage: 'The contract to hold the event in the hall was frustrated when the building was destroyed by fire.', section: 'Sec 56 Indian Contract Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Privity of Contract', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'Only parties to a contract can sue or be sued. Third parties generally have no rights under the contract.', usage: 'The sub-buyer could not sue the manufacturer directly as there was no privity of contract between them.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Quantum Meruit', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'As much as is deserved. A claim for reasonable compensation for work done when a contract is terminated.', usage: 'The contractor claimed quantum meruit for the work completed before the contract was wrongfully terminated.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Undue Influence', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'When one party uses their dominant position to obtain an unfair advantage in a contract.', usage: 'The elderly parent\'s property deed was set aside as the son exercised undue influence to obtain consent.', section: 'Sec 16 Indian Contract Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Coercion', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'Committing or threatening to commit an act forbidden by law, to compel a person to enter into an agreement.', usage: 'The agreement was voidable as it was obtained by coercion — the accused threatened bodily harm.', section: 'Sec 15 Indian Contract Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Misrepresentation', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'A false statement of fact made innocently (without intent to deceive) that induces a person to enter a contract.', usage: 'The buyer rescinded the contract after discovering the seller\'s misrepresentation about the car\'s mileage.', section: 'Sec 18 Indian Contract Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Fraud', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'Intentional deception to induce a person to enter a contract. The deceived party can avoid the contract.', usage: 'The seller committed fraud by concealing the structural defects in the building.', section: 'Sec 17 Indian Contract Act'),

  // ═══ CORPORATE & COMMERCIAL ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Memorandum of Association', category: 'Corporate', meaning: 'The fundamental document defining a company\'s constitution, name, registered office, objects, and liability.', usage: 'The company cannot engage in banking as it is not within the objects clause of its Memorandum of Association.', section: 'Sec 4 Companies Act, 2013'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Articles of Association', category: 'Corporate', meaning: 'The internal rules governing the management and administration of a company.', usage: 'The Articles of Association prescribe the procedure for appointment and removal of directors.', section: 'Sec 5 Companies Act, 2013'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Director', category: 'Corporate', meaning: 'A person appointed to the board of a company to manage its affairs and take strategic decisions.', usage: 'The independent director raised concerns about the related party transaction at the board meeting.', section: 'Sec 149 Companies Act, 2013'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Shareholder', category: 'Corporate', meaning: 'A person who holds shares in a company and has ownership rights proportional to their shareholding.', usage: 'The minority shareholder filed an oppression petition under Section 241 of the Companies Act.', section: 'Sec 241 Companies Act, 2013'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Winding Up', category: 'Corporate', meaning: 'The process of dissolving a company by selling its assets, paying off debts, and distributing remainder to shareholders.', usage: 'The NCLT ordered winding up of the company as it was unable to pay its debts.', section: 'Sec 271 Companies Act, 2013'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Insolvency', category: 'Corporate', meaning: 'The state of being unable to pay debts when they become due. Triggers formal resolution processes.', usage: 'The corporate debtor was admitted into insolvency resolution under the IBC after defaulting on ₹1 crore.', section: 'Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code, 2016'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Resolution Professional', category: 'Corporate', meaning: 'A person appointed to manage the affairs of a corporate debtor during the insolvency resolution process.', usage: 'The resolution professional invited resolution plans from prospective buyers within 180 days.', section: 'Sec 22 IBC, 2016'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'NCLT', category: 'Corporate', meaning: 'National Company Law Tribunal. A quasi-judicial body adjudicating issues relating to companies and insolvency.', usage: 'The NCLT approved the resolution plan submitted by the successful bidder.', section: 'Companies Act, 2013 / IBC, 2016'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Prospectus', category: 'Corporate', meaning: 'A document issued by a company inviting the public to subscribe to its shares or debentures.', usage: 'The company issued a prospectus for its IPO disclosing all material facts to potential investors.', section: 'Sec 26 Companies Act, 2013'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Insider Trading', category: 'Corporate', meaning: 'Trading in securities based on unpublished price-sensitive information, prohibited under SEBI regulations.', usage: 'The CEO was penalized by SEBI for insider trading after buying shares before the merger announcement.', section: 'SEBI (Prohibition of Insider Trading) Regulations'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Negotiable Instrument', category: 'Corporate', meaning: 'A written document guaranteeing payment of a specific amount, transferable by delivery or endorsement.', usage: 'The cheque, being a negotiable instrument, was dishonoured due to insufficient funds.', section: 'Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Cheque Bounce', category: 'Corporate', meaning: 'Dishonour of a cheque by the bank due to insufficient funds or other reasons, constituting a criminal offence.', usage: 'The payee filed a complaint under Section 138 NI Act after the cheque was returned unpaid.', section: 'Sec 138 Negotiable Instruments Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Trademark', category: 'Corporate', meaning: 'A distinctive sign or symbol used to identify goods or services of a particular business.', usage: 'The company registered its brand logo as a trademark to prevent competitors from using a similar mark.', section: 'Trade Marks Act, 1999'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Patent', category: 'Corporate', meaning: 'An exclusive right granted for an invention, providing protection for a limited period (usually 20 years).', usage: 'The pharmaceutical company obtained a patent for its new drug formulation.', section: 'Patents Act, 1970'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Copyright', category: 'Corporate', meaning: 'The exclusive right of the creator of an original literary, artistic, or musical work to reproduce and distribute it.', usage: 'The author filed a copyright infringement suit against the publisher for unauthorized reproduction of his book.', section: 'Copyright Act, 1957'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'LLP', category: 'Corporate', meaning: 'Limited Liability Partnership. A business structure combining the flexibility of a partnership with limited liability.', usage: 'The law firm was registered as an LLP to limit partners\' liability to their agreed contribution.', section: 'Limited Liability Partnership Act, 2008'),

  // ═══ TAXATION ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Assessment', category: 'Taxation', meaning: 'The process by which the tax authority determines the tax liability of a taxpayer.', usage: 'The Assessing Officer completed the scrutiny assessment and issued a demand notice for additional tax.', section: 'Sec 143 Income Tax Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Tax Evasion', category: 'Taxation', meaning: 'The illegal act of deliberately misrepresenting or concealing information to reduce tax liability.', usage: 'The taxpayer was prosecuted for tax evasion after concealing income of ₹2 crore from undisclosed sources.', section: 'Sec 276C Income Tax Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Tax Avoidance', category: 'Taxation', meaning: 'The legal arrangement of financial affairs to minimize tax liability within the framework of the law.', usage: 'Using Section 80C deductions for tax planning is a lawful method of tax avoidance.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'TDS', category: 'Taxation', meaning: 'Tax Deducted at Source. Tax deducted by the payer at the time of making specified payments.', usage: 'The employer deducted TDS at 10% from the contractor\'s payment and deposited it with the government.', section: 'Sec 192-206 Income Tax Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'GST', category: 'Taxation', meaning: 'Goods and Services Tax. A unified indirect tax on supply of goods and services across India.', usage: 'The supplier charged 18% GST on the consulting services as per the applicable rate.', section: 'GST Acts, 2017'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Assessee', category: 'Taxation', meaning: 'A person by whom income tax or any other tax is payable under the law.', usage: 'The assessee filed a return declaring total income of ₹15,00,000 for the assessment year.', section: 'Sec 2(7) Income Tax Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Capital Gains', category: 'Taxation', meaning: 'Profit earned from the sale of a capital asset such as property, shares, or gold.', usage: 'The seller paid long-term capital gains tax at 20% on the profit from sale of the commercial property.', section: 'Sec 45 Income Tax Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Stamp Duty', category: 'Taxation', meaning: 'A tax levied by the state government on documents relating to transfer of property and other transactions.', usage: 'The sale deed was registered after payment of stamp duty at 6% of the market value of the property.', section: 'Indian Stamp Act, 1899'),

  // ═══ CYBER LAW ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Cyber Crime', category: 'Cyber', meaning: 'Criminal activities carried out using computers, networks, or the internet.', usage: 'The accused was charged with cyber crime for hacking into the bank\'s server and stealing customer data.', section: 'IT Act, 2000 / BNS'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Hacking', category: 'Cyber', meaning: 'Unauthorized access to a computer system or network to steal, alter, or destroy data.', usage: 'The hacker gained unauthorized access to the government website and defaced it.', section: 'Sec 66 IT Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Phishing', category: 'Cyber', meaning: 'A fraudulent attempt to obtain sensitive information by disguising as a trustworthy entity in electronic communication.', usage: 'The accused sent phishing emails impersonating a bank to steal login credentials from customers.', section: 'Sec 66C, 66D IT Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Identity Theft', category: 'Cyber', meaning: 'Fraudulent use of another person\'s personal data or electronic signature.', usage: 'The accused used the victim\'s Aadhaar number to open bank accounts — charged with identity theft.', section: 'Sec 66C IT Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Cyber Stalking', category: 'Cyber', meaning: 'Using electronic communication to harass, threaten, or intimidate a person repeatedly.', usage: 'The accused was charged with cyber stalking for sending hundreds of threatening messages to the victim.', section: 'Sec 67 IT Act / BNS provisions'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Data Protection', category: 'Cyber', meaning: 'Legal framework governing the collection, storage, processing, and sharing of personal data.', usage: 'The company was found in violation of data protection norms for sharing user data without consent.', section: 'Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Intermediary', category: 'Cyber', meaning: 'A person or entity that stores, transmits, or provides services related to electronic records (e.g., ISPs, social media platforms).', usage: 'The social media platform, as an intermediary, was directed to take down the defamatory content within 24 hours.', section: 'Sec 2(w) IT Act / IT Rules, 2021'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Digital Signature', category: 'Cyber', meaning: 'An electronic authentication of a document using cryptographic techniques, equivalent to a handwritten signature.', usage: 'The contract was executed using digital signatures and has the same legal validity as a physical signature.', section: 'Sec 3 IT Act'),

  // ═══ ENVIRONMENTAL LAW ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Polluter Pays Principle', category: 'Environmental', meaning: 'The entity responsible for pollution must bear the cost of managing it and compensating affected parties.', usage: 'The factory was ordered to pay ₹50 crore compensation under the polluter pays principle for contaminating the river.', section: 'Environment Protection Act, 1986'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Precautionary Principle', category: 'Environmental', meaning: 'When an activity threatens harm to the environment, precautionary measures should be taken even without full scientific certainty.', usage: 'The court applied the precautionary principle and directed an environmental impact assessment before approving the project.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Public Trust Doctrine', category: 'Environmental', meaning: 'The State holds certain natural resources (air, water, forests) in trust for the public and cannot permit their destruction.', usage: 'The court invoked the public trust doctrine to prevent privatization of a lake for commercial construction.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Environmental Impact Assessment', category: 'Environmental', meaning: 'A process of evaluating the likely environmental impacts of a proposed project before granting approval.', usage: 'The mining project was halted as no EIA clearance was obtained from the Ministry of Environment.', section: 'EIA Notification, 2006'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'NGT', category: 'Environmental', meaning: 'National Green Tribunal. A specialized tribunal for expeditious disposal of cases relating to environmental protection.', usage: 'The NGT imposed a fine of ₹5 crore on the company for dumping industrial waste into the river.', section: 'National Green Tribunal Act, 2010'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Forest Conservation', category: 'Environmental', meaning: 'Laws restricting diversion of forest land for non-forest purposes without Central government approval.', usage: 'The highway project was stayed as forest clearance under the Forest Conservation Act was not obtained.', section: 'Forest Conservation Act, 1980'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Wildlife Protection', category: 'Environmental', meaning: 'Laws prohibiting hunting, poaching, and trade of endangered species and their products.', usage: 'The accused was arrested for poaching a tiger in the national park.', section: 'Wildlife Protection Act, 1972'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Sustainable Development', category: 'Environmental', meaning: 'Development that meets the needs of the present without compromising the ability of future generations to meet their needs.', usage: 'The Supreme Court upheld the principle of sustainable development while balancing industrial growth with environmental protection.'),

  // ═══ LABOUR LAW ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Retrenchment', category: 'Labour', meaning: 'Termination of a workman\'s service by the employer for any reason other than disciplinary action.', usage: 'The employer retrenched 50 workers without following the last-in-first-out principle required by law.', section: 'Sec 25F Industrial Disputes Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Strike', category: 'Labour', meaning: 'A concerted refusal by workers to work, as a form of protest against the employer.', usage: 'The trade union called a strike demanding increase in wages and improvement in working conditions.', section: 'Sec 2(q) Industrial Disputes Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Lockout', category: 'Labour', meaning: 'Closure of a place of employment or suspension of work by the employer to compel workers to accept terms.', usage: 'The factory owner declared a lockout after the workers refused to accept the new shift timings.', section: 'Sec 2(l) Industrial Disputes Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Industrial Dispute', category: 'Labour', meaning: 'Any dispute between employers and employees relating to employment, conditions of work, or terms of employment.', usage: 'The dispute over non-payment of bonus was referred to the Labour Court for adjudication.', section: 'Industrial Disputes Act, 1947'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Gratuity', category: 'Labour', meaning: 'A lump sum amount paid by the employer to an employee upon retirement or termination after 5 years of service.', usage: 'The employee received gratuity of ₹10,00,000 after completing 20 years of continuous service.', section: 'Payment of Gratuity Act, 1972'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Provident Fund', category: 'Labour', meaning: 'A compulsory savings scheme where both employer and employee contribute monthly towards retirement benefits.', usage: 'The employer was penalized for failure to deposit the employees\' PF contribution with the EPFO.', section: 'Employees\' Provident Funds Act, 1952'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Minimum Wages', category: 'Labour', meaning: 'The lowest amount of wages that an employer is legally required to pay to workers.', usage: 'The employer was directed to pay arrears of minimum wages as he had been paying below the notified rate.', section: 'Minimum Wages Act, 1948'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Workman', category: 'Labour', meaning: 'A person employed in any industry to do skilled, unskilled, manual, operational, or clerical work for hire.', usage: 'The supervisor was held to be a workman under the Industrial Disputes Act as his duties were primarily manual.', section: 'Sec 2(s) Industrial Disputes Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Lay Off', category: 'Labour', meaning: 'Temporary suspension of employment by the employer due to shortage of raw materials, power, or natural calamity.', usage: 'The factory laid off workers for two weeks due to shortage of raw materials and paid lay-off compensation.', section: 'Sec 25C Industrial Disputes Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Unfair Labour Practice', category: 'Labour', meaning: 'Actions by an employer or trade union that violate workers\' rights or undermine collective bargaining.', usage: 'Threatening workers with dismissal for joining a union constitutes an unfair labour practice.', section: 'Sec 25T Industrial Disputes Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Equal Pay for Equal Work', category: 'Labour', meaning: 'The principle that workers performing the same work should receive the same remuneration regardless of gender.', usage: 'The female employees filed a complaint claiming violation of equal pay for equal work principle.', section: 'Equal Remuneration Act / Article 39(d) Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Sexual Harassment at Workplace', category: 'Labour', meaning: 'Unwelcome sexual conduct at the workplace including physical contact, demand for sexual favours, or sexually coloured remarks.', usage: 'An Internal Complaints Committee was constituted under the POSH Act to investigate the allegation of sexual harassment.', section: 'POSH Act, 2013'),

  // ═══ ADDITIONAL LEGAL ENGLISH ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Affirmation', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A solemn declaration made in place of an oath by persons who object to taking an oath.', usage: 'The witness made an affirmation instead of taking an oath on religious grounds before giving testimony.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Attestation', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The act of witnessing the execution of a document and signing it as proof.', usage: 'The will was attested by two witnesses who were present when the testator signed the document.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Bequeath', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'To leave personal property to someone by means of a will.', usage: 'The testator bequeathed his entire art collection to the national museum.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Bonafide Purchaser', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A person who purchases property in good faith, for value, without notice of any defect in the seller\'s title.', usage: 'The court protected the rights of the bonafide purchaser who had no knowledge of the prior dispute.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Codicil', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A supplement or addition to a will, modifying, explaining, or revoking provisions of the original will.', usage: 'The testator added a codicil to his will, changing the beneficiary of his bank accounts.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Collusion', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A secret agreement between two or more persons to deceive the court or obtain an unfair advantage.', usage: 'The divorce was denied as the court suspected collusion between the parties to obtain a fraudulent decree.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Condonation', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'Forgiveness or pardon for a legal wrong, often delay in filing.', usage: 'The court condoned the delay of 30 days in filing the appeal as the applicant showed sufficient cause.', section: 'Sec 5 Limitation Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Constructive Notice', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'Knowledge imputed to a person by law, regardless of whether they actually knew the fact.', usage: 'Registration of a document constitutes constructive notice to all persons of its contents.', section: 'Sec 3 Transfer of Property Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Contributory Negligence', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'When the injured party\'s own negligence contributed to the harm, reducing the compensation awarded.', usage: 'The compensation was reduced by 30% due to contributory negligence of the victim who crossed a busy highway without looking.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Debenture', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A document acknowledging a debt, issued by a company as a long-term borrowing instrument.', usage: 'The company issued secured debentures of ₹100 crore to raise funds for expansion.', section: 'Sec 71 Companies Act, 2013'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Demurrer', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'An objection that admits the facts alleged but disputes their legal sufficiency to constitute a cause of action.', usage: 'The defendant filed a demurrer arguing that even if all facts in the plaint were true, no legal cause of action arises.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Devolution', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The transfer of property or rights from one person to another by operation of law.', usage: 'On death of the owner, the property devolved on the Class I legal heirs under the Hindu Succession Act.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Diligence', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The degree of care and caution required of a person in a given situation.', usage: 'The court found the bank liable for failing to exercise due diligence before sanctioning the fraudulent loan.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Eminent Domain', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The power of the State to acquire private property for public purpose upon payment of fair compensation.', usage: 'The government exercised eminent domain to acquire farmland for building a national highway.', section: 'Right to Fair Compensation and Transparency in Land Acquisition Act, 2013'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Fiduciary', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A person holding a position of trust and confidence, required to act in the best interest of another.', usage: 'A director owes fiduciary duties to the company and must not use company assets for personal gain.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Foreclosure', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A process by which a mortgagee takes possession of the mortgaged property when the borrower fails to repay.', usage: 'The bank initiated foreclosure proceedings after the borrower defaulted on EMI payments for six consecutive months.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Habitual Offender', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A person who has been convicted of criminal offences on multiple occasions, subject to enhanced punishment.', usage: 'The accused was declared a habitual offender with five previous convictions for burglary.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Impugn', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'To challenge or call into question the validity of a judgment, order, or action.', usage: 'The petitioner impugned the Tribunal order on the ground that it was passed without jurisdiction.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Injunction (Permanent)', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A final court order permanently restraining a party from performing a specific act.', usage: 'A permanent injunction was granted restraining the defendant from using the plaintiff\'s trademark.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Injunction (Temporary)', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'An interim court order restraining a party from performing an act until the final disposal of the suit.', usage: 'The court granted a temporary injunction preventing construction on the disputed land pending trial.', section: 'Order 39 CPC'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Intestacy', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The condition of dying without leaving a valid will, causing property to pass by law to heirs.', usage: 'On intestacy, the Hindu male\'s property passes first to Class I heirs under the Hindu Succession Act.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Locus', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The place or location where an event occurred or a cause of action arose.', usage: 'The locus of the crime was established through GPS data and witness testimony.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Moot', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A debatable point or one that has become academic as the issue no longer requires resolution.', usage: 'The petition became moot as the impugned order was already withdrawn by the government.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Nolle Prosequi', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A formal entry by the prosecution declaring that they will not proceed with the case.', usage: 'The prosecution entered nolle prosequi after the key witness recanted his testimony.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Perjury', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The offence of deliberately giving false evidence while under oath in court.', usage: 'The witness was prosecuted for perjury after CCTV footage contradicted his sworn testimony.', section: 'BNS Sec 229'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Prerogative', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'An exclusive right or privilege belonging to a person or body by virtue of their office or position.', usage: 'Granting pardon is the prerogative of the President under Article 72 of the Constitution.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Receiver', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A person appointed by the court to take charge of property or business that is the subject of litigation.', usage: 'The court appointed a receiver to manage the partnership firm pending the dissolution suit.', section: 'Order 40 CPC'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Recusal', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The act of a judge withdrawing from hearing a case due to conflict of interest or bias.', usage: 'The judge recused himself from the case as the advocate appearing was his former law partner.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Review', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A re-examination of a court\'s own order or judgment on the basis of an error apparent on the face of the record.', usage: 'A review petition was filed pointing out a manifest error in the Supreme Court judgment.', section: 'Sec 114 CPC / Order 47 CPC'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Sanction', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'Permission or approval from a competent authority, required before prosecuting certain offences or persons.', usage: 'Prosecution of the public servant for corruption requires prior sanction under the Prevention of Corruption Act.', section: 'Sec 218 BNSS / PC Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Subrogation', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The substitution of one party for another in respect of a claim against a third party.', usage: 'After paying the insurance claim, the insurer was subrogated to the insured\'s rights against the negligent driver.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Testimony', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A formal statement made by a witness under oath in court.', usage: 'The eyewitness testimony was the most crucial evidence in establishing the accused\'s presence at the crime scene.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Tribunal', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A quasi-judicial body established by law to adjudicate specific disputes outside the regular court system.', usage: 'The dispute was referred to the Income Tax Appellate Tribunal for adjudication.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Vicarious Liability', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'Liability imposed on one person for the acts of another, typically an employer for acts of employees.', usage: 'The hospital was held vicariously liable for the negligence of its employed surgeon during surgery.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Winding Up Petition', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A petition filed before the NCLT seeking the dissolution of a company that is unable to pay its debts.', usage: 'The creditor filed a winding up petition as the company failed to pay the outstanding debt of ₹2 crore.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Zero FIR', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'An FIR that can be filed at any police station regardless of jurisdiction where the crime occurred.', usage: 'The victim filed a Zero FIR at the nearest police station, which was later transferred to the jurisdictional station.', section: 'Sec 173(1) BNSS'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Lok Adalat', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'People\'s Court. A forum for alternative dispute resolution where cases are settled by compromise.', usage: 'The motor accident claim was settled at the Lok Adalat, saving time and costs for both parties.', section: 'Legal Services Authorities Act, 1987'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Legal Aid', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'Free legal services provided to persons who cannot afford legal representation.', usage: 'The accused was provided free legal aid through the District Legal Services Authority as he could not afford a lawyer.', section: 'Article 39A Constitution / Legal Services Authorities Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Amend', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'To formally change or modify a pleading, order, or statute.', usage: 'The plaintiff sought leave to amend the plaint to include an additional cause of action discovered during trial.', section: 'Order 6 Rule 17 CPC'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Enclosure', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A document or exhibit attached to and forming part of a legal filing or pleading.', usage: 'The petition was filed with 15 enclosures including affidavits, documents, and photographs.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Discovery', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A pre-trial procedure requiring parties to disclose documents and facts relevant to the case.', usage: 'The court ordered discovery and inspection of the defendant\'s financial records.', section: 'Order 11 CPC'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Commission', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A direction by the court to a person (commissioner) to perform specific tasks like examining a witness or inspecting property.', usage: 'The court issued a commission to the Advocate Commissioner to inspect the disputed property and file a report.', section: 'Order 26 CPC'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Advocate Commissioner', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'An advocate appointed by the court to inspect property, record evidence, or perform other specific tasks on behalf of the court.', usage: 'The Advocate Commissioner conducted a site inspection and submitted a detailed report with photographs and GPS coordinates.', section: 'Order 26 CPC'),

  // ═══ ADDITIONAL LATIN MAXIMS ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Ab Initio', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'From the beginning. Used to indicate that something is invalid from its inception.', usage: 'The contract was declared void ab initio as one party was a minor at the time of execution.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Actio Personalis Moritur Cum Persona', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'A personal action dies with the person. Certain legal actions cannot survive the death of a party.', usage: 'The defamation suit abated on death of the plaintiff as actio personalis moritur cum persona applies.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Animus Possidendi', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'Intention to possess. An essential element for claiming adverse possession.', usage: 'The claimant must prove both physical possession and animus possidendi to succeed in adverse possession.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Autrefois Acquit', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'Previously acquitted. A plea that the accused has already been tried and acquitted for the same offence.', usage: 'The accused raised the plea of autrefois acquit, producing the earlier acquittal order for the same transaction.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Autrefois Convict', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'Previously convicted. A plea that the accused has already been convicted for the same offence.', usage: 'The second prosecution was barred under the plea of autrefois convict.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Bona Vacantia', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'Ownerless goods. Property that has no apparent owner and passes to the State.', usage: 'The property of the deceased who left no heirs or will became bona vacantia and vested in the government.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Casus Omissus', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'A case omitted. A situation not covered by a statute that the legislature failed to provide for.', usage: 'The court cannot fill a casus omissus in a taxing statute by interpretation — it must be left to the legislature.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Cessante Ratione Legis Cessat Ipsa Lex', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'When the reason for the law ceases, the law itself ceases.', usage: 'The restriction imposed during wartime was lifted as the reason for the law had ceased with the end of hostilities.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Contemporanea Expositio', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'Contemporary interpretation. A statute should be interpreted according to its meaning at the time of enactment.', usage: 'The ancient statute was interpreted using contemporanea expositio to understand the original legislative intent.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Delegatus Non Potest Delegare', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'A delegate cannot further delegate. A person entrusted with power cannot give that power to another.', usage: 'The Commissioner could not sub-delegate the power of inspection to his subordinate as delegatus non potest delegare.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Ex Gratia', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'Out of grace. A payment made voluntarily without legal obligation, often as goodwill or compassion.', usage: 'The government announced ex gratia payment of ₹5,00,000 to the families of flood victims.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Ex Officio', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'By virtue of office. Powers or rights held automatically because of holding a particular position.', usage: 'The Vice-President is the ex officio Chairman of the Rajya Sabha.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Fiat Justitia Ruat Caelum', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'Let justice be done though the heavens fall. Justice must be administered regardless of consequences.', usage: 'The court held that fiat justitia ruat caelum — no political consideration can stand in the way of justice.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Generalia Specialibus Non Derogant', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'General provisions do not override special provisions. A specific law prevails over a general law.', usage: 'The special provision of the Rent Control Act prevails over the general provisions of the Transfer of Property Act.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'In Pari Delicto', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'In equal fault. Both parties are equally at fault, and neither can claim relief against the other.', usage: 'As both parties were in pari delicto in the illegal transaction, the court refused relief to either.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Jus Naturale', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'Natural law. A system of law based on fundamental ideas of right and wrong inherent in human nature.', usage: 'The right to self-defence is recognized as part of jus naturale across all legal systems.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Lex Fori', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'The law of the forum. The procedural law of the court where the case is being tried.', usage: 'Although the contract was governed by English law, the procedural aspects were determined by lex fori — Indian law.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Lex Loci', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'The law of the place. The law applicable based on the location where the act occurred or contract was made.', usage: 'The validity of the marriage was determined by lex loci — the law of the country where it was solemnized.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Nemo Dat Quod Non Habet', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'No one can give what they do not have. A seller cannot transfer better title than they possess.', usage: 'The buyer of stolen goods acquired no title as the seller had none to transfer — nemo dat quod non habet.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Per Incuriam', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'Through lack of care. A decision made in ignorance of relevant statutory provision or binding authority.', usage: 'The judgment was held per incuriam as the bench was not aware of the Supreme Court decision directly on point.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Restitutio In Integrum', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'Restoration to the original position. The remedy of restoring a party to the position they were in before the wrong.', usage: 'The court ordered restitutio in integrum, directing the defendant to return the land and pay compensation.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Salus Populi Suprema Lex', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'The welfare of the people is the supreme law.', usage: 'The court invoked salus populi suprema lex in upholding the government\'s decision to lock down during the pandemic.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Suppressio Veri', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'Suppression of truth. Concealing material facts amounts to fraud.', usage: 'The insurance claim was denied due to suppressio veri — the insured concealed his pre-existing medical condition.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Suggestio Falsi', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'Suggestion of falsehood. Making a false representation amounts to fraud.', usage: 'The contract was voidable for suggestio falsi as the seller falsely claimed the diamond was natural.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Terra Nullius', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'Land belonging to no one. Uninhabited territory that can be claimed by a state.', usage: 'The concept of terra nullius was historically used to justify colonization of indigenous lands.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Turpi Causa', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'From a dishonourable cause. A claim founded on an immoral or illegal act cannot be enforced.', usage: 'The court refused to enforce the agreement as it arose ex turpi causa — from an illegal gambling transaction.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Uberrimae Fidei', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'Of the utmost good faith. Insurance contracts require the highest degree of honesty by both parties.', usage: 'The insurance policy was voided as the insured failed to disclose a material fact — uberrimae fidei was violated.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Veto', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'I forbid. The constitutional right of the President or Governor to refuse assent to a bill.', usage: 'The President exercised the pocket veto by neither signing nor returning the bill to Parliament.'),

  // ═══ CONSUMER LAW ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Consumer', category: 'Consumer', meaning: 'A person who buys goods or hires services for consideration, excluding commercial resale.', usage: 'The patient who paid for medical treatment is a consumer entitled to protection under the Consumer Protection Act.', section: 'Sec 2(7) Consumer Protection Act, 2019'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Consumer Dispute', category: 'Consumer', meaning: 'A dispute between a consumer and a seller/service provider regarding defective goods, deficient service, or unfair trade practice.', usage: 'The consumer filed a complaint before the District Commission for deficiency in service by the hospital.', section: 'Sec 2(8) Consumer Protection Act, 2019'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Deficiency in Service', category: 'Consumer', meaning: 'Any fault, imperfection, or shortcoming in the quality, nature, or manner of service provided.', usage: 'The bank\'s failure to process the loan within the promised timeframe amounted to deficiency in service.', section: 'Sec 2(11) Consumer Protection Act, 2019'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Defective Goods', category: 'Consumer', meaning: 'Goods that do not conform to the standard agreed upon or are faulty in design, manufacturing, or quality.', usage: 'The car was returned as defective goods after the engine failed within one month of purchase.', section: 'Sec 2(10) Consumer Protection Act, 2019'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Unfair Trade Practice', category: 'Consumer', meaning: 'Misleading advertisements, false representation, or deceptive practices in the sale of goods or services.', usage: 'The company\'s advertisement claiming the product cured cancer was held to be an unfair trade practice.', section: 'Sec 2(47) Consumer Protection Act, 2019'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Product Liability', category: 'Consumer', meaning: 'The responsibility of a manufacturer, seller, or service provider for any harm caused by a defective product.', usage: 'The company was held liable under product liability for injuries caused by the exploding battery.', section: 'Sec 82-87 Consumer Protection Act, 2019'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'CCPA', category: 'Consumer', meaning: 'Central Consumer Protection Authority. A regulatory body to promote, protect, and enforce consumer rights.', usage: 'The CCPA issued directions to the e-commerce platform to stop misleading advertisements.', section: 'Sec 10 Consumer Protection Act, 2019'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Consumer Forum', category: 'Consumer', meaning: 'A quasi-judicial body set up at district, state, and national levels to resolve consumer disputes.', usage: 'The consumer filed a complaint before the District Consumer Disputes Redressal Forum seeking refund and compensation.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Restrictive Trade Practice', category: 'Consumer', meaning: 'Business practices that restrict competition, manipulate prices, or limit the supply of goods.', usage: 'The manufacturer\'s insistence on exclusive dealership was challenged as a restrictive trade practice.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Caveat Venditor', category: 'Consumer', meaning: 'Let the seller beware. The seller is responsible for the quality of goods sold.', usage: 'Under the Consumer Protection Act, the principle has shifted from caveat emptor to caveat venditor — the seller must ensure quality.'),

  // ═══ ADMINISTRATIVE LAW ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Natural Justice', category: 'Administrative', meaning: 'Principles of fairness in legal proceedings: the right to be heard and the rule against bias.', usage: 'The dismissal order was quashed for violation of natural justice as the employee was not given a hearing.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Delegated Legislation', category: 'Administrative', meaning: 'Rules, regulations, and bye-laws made by the executive under the authority delegated by the legislature.', usage: 'The bye-laws framed by the municipality under the Municipal Act are a form of delegated legislation.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Administrative Tribunal', category: 'Administrative', meaning: 'A tribunal established to adjudicate disputes relating to recruitment and service conditions of government employees.', usage: 'The government employee challenged his transfer order before the Central Administrative Tribunal.', section: 'Administrative Tribunals Act, 1985'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Legitimate Expectation', category: 'Administrative', meaning: 'A reasonable expectation of a benefit arising from a past practice or promise by a public authority.', usage: 'The contractual employees had a legitimate expectation of regularization based on the government\'s previous policy.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Wednesbury Unreasonableness', category: 'Administrative', meaning: 'A decision so unreasonable that no reasonable authority could have made it. Standard for reviewing administrative decisions.', usage: 'The court set aside the transfer order as Wednesbury unreasonable since it was punitive and not in public interest.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Proportionality', category: 'Administrative', meaning: 'A principle requiring that administrative action be proportionate to the objective sought to be achieved.', usage: 'Dismissal from service for a minor clerical error was disproportionate to the offence — the court reduced the punishment.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'RTI', category: 'Administrative', meaning: 'Right to Information. The right of citizens to obtain information from public authorities to promote transparency.', usage: 'The activist filed an RTI application seeking details of the government expenditure on the road project.', section: 'Right to Information Act, 2005'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Ombudsman', category: 'Administrative', meaning: 'An independent official appointed to investigate complaints against government departments or public bodies.', usage: 'The banking ombudsman resolved the customer\'s complaint regarding unauthorized debit from their account.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Quasi-Judicial', category: 'Administrative', meaning: 'Relating to a body that has powers similar to a court but is not a regular court, such as tribunals and commissions.', usage: 'The Labour Commissioner acts in a quasi-judicial capacity when adjudicating disputes under the Payment of Wages Act.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Statutory Body', category: 'Administrative', meaning: 'A body established by an Act of Parliament or State Legislature with specific powers and functions.', usage: 'SEBI is a statutory body established under the SEBI Act, 1992 to regulate the securities market.'),

  // ═══ INTERNATIONAL LAW ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Extradition', category: 'International', meaning: 'The formal process of surrendering a person accused or convicted of a crime to the jurisdiction where the offence occurred.', usage: 'India requested extradition of the fugitive economic offender from the UK under the bilateral extradition treaty.', section: 'Extradition Act, 1962'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Diplomatic Immunity', category: 'International', meaning: 'Protection of foreign diplomats from prosecution or lawsuit in the host country.', usage: 'The ambassador could not be prosecuted for the traffic violation due to diplomatic immunity under the Vienna Convention.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Treaty', category: 'International', meaning: 'A formal agreement between two or more sovereign states governed by international law.', usage: 'India signed a bilateral treaty with Australia for mutual legal assistance in criminal matters.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Asylum', category: 'International', meaning: 'Protection granted by a state to a foreign national who is fleeing persecution in their home country.', usage: 'The political dissident sought asylum in the Indian embassy claiming persecution by his home government.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Sovereignty', category: 'International', meaning: 'The supreme authority of a state to govern itself without external interference.', usage: 'The court upheld India\'s sovereignty in refusing to submit to the jurisdiction of a foreign tribunal.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Refugee', category: 'International', meaning: 'A person who has fled their country due to persecution, war, or violence and cannot return safely.', usage: 'The refugees from the neighbouring country were given temporary shelter and basic amenities by the Indian government.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Geneva Convention', category: 'International', meaning: 'International treaties establishing standards for humanitarian treatment during war, protecting civilians and prisoners of war.', usage: 'The treatment of prisoners of war must comply with the Geneva Conventions, ensuring humane conditions.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Interpol Red Notice', category: 'International', meaning: 'An international request to locate and provisionally arrest a person pending extradition or similar legal action.', usage: 'An Interpol Red Notice was issued against the accused who fled abroad after committing a financial fraud.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Mutual Legal Assistance', category: 'International', meaning: 'Cooperation between countries in gathering and exchanging evidence for criminal investigations and proceedings.', usage: 'India sent a request for mutual legal assistance to gather evidence from banks in Singapore.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'International Court of Justice', category: 'International', meaning: 'The principal judicial organ of the United Nations, settling legal disputes between states.', usage: 'India filed a case before the ICJ seeking stay of execution of its national sentenced to death in Pakistan.'),

  // ═══ ADDITIONAL CRIMINAL TERMS ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Cognizance', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'The formal act of a Magistrate taking notice of an offence and initiating judicial proceedings.', usage: 'The Magistrate took cognizance of the offence upon receiving the police report.', section: 'Sec 210 BNSS'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Committal', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'The process of transferring a case from the Magistrate\'s Court to the Sessions Court for trial.', usage: 'The case of murder was committed to the Sessions Court as the Magistrate had no jurisdiction to try it.', section: 'Sec 232 BNSS'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Compoundable Offence', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'An offence that can be settled between the complainant and accused without requiring court permission.', usage: 'Simple hurt is a compoundable offence — the injured party can compromise and withdraw the case.', section: 'Sec 359 BNSS'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Default Bail', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Bail granted as a right when the investigation is not completed, and chargesheet is not filed within the statutory period.', usage: 'The accused was entitled to default bail as the chargesheet was not filed within 90 days.', section: 'Sec 187 BNSS'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Detention', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'The act of keeping a person in custody by authorities. Can be preventive or punitive.', usage: 'The preventive detention order was challenged as the grounds were vague and not communicated to the detenu.', section: 'Article 22 Constitution / National Security Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Evidence Tampering', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'The act of illegally altering, destroying, or concealing evidence relevant to a case.', usage: 'The accused was charged with evidence tampering after CCTV footage showed him removing documents from the crime scene.', section: 'BNS Sec 238'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Juvenile', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'A person below the age of 18 years, who is dealt with under a separate legal framework focused on rehabilitation.', usage: 'The 16-year-old accused was treated as a juvenile and produced before the Juvenile Justice Board.', section: 'Juvenile Justice Act, 2015'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Lookout Circular', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'A notice issued by authorities to immigration officials at airports and borders to prevent a person from leaving the country.', usage: 'A lookout circular was issued against the accused to prevent him from fleeing outside India.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Magistrate', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'A judicial officer with limited criminal jurisdiction, including power to try certain offences and record confessions.', usage: 'The accused was produced before the Judicial Magistrate First Class within 24 hours of arrest.', section: 'Sec 16-24 BNSS'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Non-Bailable Offence', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'An offence where bail is not a right and can only be granted at the discretion of the court.', usage: 'Murder is a non-bailable offence; the accused must apply to the court for bail.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Proclamation', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'A public declaration by the court requiring an absconding accused to appear before it within a specified time.', usage: 'The court issued a proclamation under Section 84 BNSS directing the absconding accused to appear within 30 days.', section: 'Sec 84 BNSS'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Prosecution Sanction', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'Prior approval required from the government before prosecuting a public servant for acts done in official capacity.', usage: 'The prosecution was quashed as no valid sanction was obtained before filing the case against the government officer.', section: 'Sec 218 BNSS'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Punishment', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'A penalty imposed by the court upon conviction, including imprisonment, fine, community service, or death sentence.', usage: 'The court sentenced the accused to 7 years rigorous imprisonment and a fine of ₹50,000.', section: 'BNS Sec 4'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Self-Defence', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'The right of a person to use reasonable force to protect themselves or others from imminent unlawful harm.', usage: 'The accused was acquitted on the ground of self-defence as the deceased attacked him with a knife first.', section: 'BNS Sec 34-44'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Sessions Court', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'A court presided over by a Sessions Judge with jurisdiction to try serious criminal offences including murder.', usage: 'The murder case was tried before the Additional Sessions Judge who has power to impose the death sentence.', section: 'Sec 19 BNSS'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Summary Trial', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'A simplified and faster trial procedure used for petty offences carrying punishment up to 2 years.', usage: 'The case of petty theft was tried summarily and disposed of in a single hearing.', section: 'Sec 283-289 BNSS'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Surety Bond', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'A bond executed by a person guaranteeing the appearance of the accused in court.', usage: 'Two persons of good standing executed surety bonds of ₹50,000 each for the accused\'s bail.'),

  // ═══ ADDITIONAL PROPERTY & CIVIL ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Attachment', category: 'Property', meaning: 'Seizure of property by court order to prevent its disposal, used in both civil execution and criminal proceedings.', usage: 'The court ordered attachment of the defendant\'s bank account and immovable property before judgment.', section: 'Order 38 CPC'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Conveyance', category: 'Property', meaning: 'The legal process of transferring ownership of immovable property from one person to another.', usage: 'The conveyance deed was executed and registered, completing the transfer of the flat to the buyer.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Demarcation', category: 'Property', meaning: 'The process of determining and marking the boundaries of a property.', usage: 'A survey was ordered for demarcation of the boundary between the two adjacent agricultural lands.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Hypothecation', category: 'Property', meaning: 'A pledge of movable property as security for a loan without transferring possession to the lender.', usage: 'The car was hypothecated to the bank as security for the vehicle loan. The borrower retains possession.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Injunction (Mandatory)', category: 'Property', meaning: 'A court order compelling a party to perform a specific act, such as restoring the status quo.', usage: 'A mandatory injunction was granted directing the defendant to demolish the wall blocking the plaintiff\'s pathway.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Khata', category: 'Property', meaning: 'A property tax document maintained by the municipal authority recording the owner\'s name, property details, and tax liability.', usage: 'The khata was transferred to the buyer\'s name after producing the registered sale deed at the municipal office.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Patta', category: 'Property', meaning: 'A land ownership document issued by the revenue department certifying the holder as the legal owner.', usage: 'The farmer produced the patta (land title certificate) issued by the government as proof of ownership.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Power of Sale', category: 'Property', meaning: 'The right of a mortgagee to sell the mortgaged property without court intervention upon default.', usage: 'The bank exercised its power of sale under the SARFAESI Act and auctioned the property after the borrower defaulted.', section: 'SARFAESI Act, 2002'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Pre-emption', category: 'Property', meaning: 'The right of a person (typically a co-owner or neighbour) to purchase property before it is sold to a third party.', usage: 'The co-sharer exercised his right of pre-emption to purchase the share being sold to an outsider.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Rectification of Deed', category: 'Property', meaning: 'Correction of errors or inaccuracies in a registered document through a supplementary deed.', usage: 'A rectification deed was executed to correct the misspelling of the buyer\'s name in the original sale deed.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Redemption', category: 'Property', meaning: 'The right of a mortgagor to reclaim the mortgaged property by repaying the debt in full.', usage: 'The borrower exercised the right of redemption by repaying the entire loan amount to recover the pledged property.', section: 'Sec 60 Transfer of Property Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Surrender', category: 'Property', meaning: 'The yielding up of a lease or tenancy by the tenant to the landlord before its expiry.', usage: 'The tenant surrendered the premises voluntarily and handed over the keys to the landlord.', section: 'Sec 111 Transfer of Property Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Trespass', category: 'Property', meaning: 'Unauthorized entry upon or interference with another person\'s land or property.', usage: 'The plaintiff filed a suit for permanent injunction against trespass by the neighbouring landowner.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Usufruct', category: 'Property', meaning: 'The right to use and enjoy the fruits of another\'s property without damaging or destroying it.', usage: 'The life tenant has a usufructuary right — she may enjoy the rental income but cannot sell the property.'),

  // ═══ ADDITIONAL CONSTITUTIONAL ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Writ of Prohibition', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'A writ issued by a higher court to prevent a lower court or tribunal from exceeding its jurisdiction.', usage: 'The High Court issued a writ of prohibition to stop the tribunal from hearing a matter outside its competence.', section: 'Article 226 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Article 32', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'The right to move the Supreme Court for enforcement of fundamental rights. Termed the "heart and soul" of the Constitution by Dr. Ambedkar.', usage: 'The petitioner filed a writ petition under Article 32 seeking enforcement of the right to equality.', section: 'Article 32 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Article 226', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'The power of High Courts to issue writs for enforcement of fundamental rights and for any other purpose.', usage: 'Article 226 confers wider jurisdiction on High Courts compared to Article 32, as it covers rights beyond fundamental rights.', section: 'Article 226 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Colourable Legislation', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'A law that appears valid on its face but is in substance beyond the legislative competence of the enacting body.', usage: 'The State Act was struck down as colourable legislation since it was essentially on a Union List subject disguised as a State subject.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Doctrine of Eclipse', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'A pre-constitutional law inconsistent with fundamental rights is not void but remains eclipsed — it revives if the fundamental right is amended.', usage: 'The pre-independence law was eclipsed by Article 19 but would revive if the relevant fundamental right is amended.', section: 'Article 13 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Doctrine of Severability', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'If part of a statute is unconstitutional, only that part is void; the rest of the statute remains valid.', usage: 'The court applied severability and struck down only Section 377 to the extent it criminalized consensual adult relations.', section: 'Article 13 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Money Bill', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'A bill dealing exclusively with taxation, government expenditure, or borrowing, which can only be introduced in the Lok Sabha.', usage: 'The Rajya Sabha can only recommend amendments to a Money Bill; Lok Sabha may accept or reject them.', section: 'Article 110 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'No Confidence Motion', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'A motion moved in the Lok Sabha to test the confidence of the ruling government; if passed, the government must resign.', usage: 'The opposition moved a no confidence motion against the government, which was defeated by a margin of 20 votes.', section: 'Rule 198 Rules of Procedure'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Privilege Motion', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'A motion raised in the legislature when a member feels their parliamentary privileges have been breached.', usage: 'A privilege motion was moved against the minister for misleading the House with incorrect data.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Schedule', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'An appendix to the Constitution containing detailed provisions. The Indian Constitution has 12 Schedules.', usage: 'The Seventh Schedule distributes legislative powers between the Union and State governments.', section: 'Schedules 1-12 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Special Leave Petition (SLP)', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'A petition to the Supreme Court seeking special permission to appeal against any judgment of any court or tribunal.', usage: 'The petitioner filed an SLP under Article 136 challenging the High Court\'s order dismissing his writ petition.', section: 'Article 136 Constitution'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Concurrent List', category: 'Constitutional', meaning: 'List III of the Seventh Schedule containing subjects on which both Parliament and State Legislature can make laws.', usage: 'Education falls under the Concurrent List — both Centre and States can legislate, but Central law prevails in case of conflict.', section: 'Seventh Schedule Constitution'),

  // ═══ FINAL ADDITIONS ═══
  LegalTerm(term: 'Novation', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'The substitution of a new contract for an existing one, or the replacement of a party to the contract.', usage: 'The original contract between A and B was novated when C replaced B as the new party, with consent of all.', section: 'Sec 62 Indian Contract Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Locus Delicti', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'The place of the offence. The location where the crime was committed, determining jurisdiction.', usage: 'The court at the locus delicti — the city where the fraud was committed — had jurisdiction to try the case.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Causa Mortis', category: 'Latin', meaning: 'In contemplation of death. A gift made in anticipation of imminent death.', usage: 'The gift of jewellery was made causa mortis by the terminally ill mother to her daughter.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Duress', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'Threats or coercion used to compel a person to enter into a contract against their will.', usage: 'The agreement signed under duress — at gunpoint — was declared voidable at the option of the aggrieved party.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Accord and Satisfaction', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'A settlement of a claim by accepting less than what is due, as agreed by both parties.', usage: 'The creditor accepted ₹80,000 in full and final settlement of the ₹1,00,000 debt — accord and satisfaction.', section: 'Sec 63 Indian Contract Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Unjust Enrichment', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A benefit obtained by one party at the expense of another without legal justification, creating an obligation to repay.', usage: 'The court ordered the defendant to return the overpayment on the principle of unjust enrichment.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Chattel', category: 'Property', meaning: 'Any movable personal property, as distinguished from real property (land and buildings).', usage: 'The furniture and electronics in the rented premises are chattels belonging to the tenant.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Moratorium', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A legally authorized period of delay in the performance of an obligation or payment of a debt.', usage: 'The RBI declared a moratorium on the stressed bank, restricting withdrawals to protect depositors.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Quorum', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'The minimum number of members required to be present for a meeting or proceeding to be validly conducted.', usage: 'The board meeting could not proceed as the quorum of five directors was not present.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Rescission', category: 'Contract', meaning: 'The cancellation or annulment of a contract, restoring parties to their pre-contractual positions.', usage: 'The buyer sought rescission of the sale agreement due to the seller\'s misrepresentation about the property.', section: 'Sec 27 Specific Relief Act'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Abscond', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'To flee or hide from law enforcement or court proceedings to avoid arrest or trial.', usage: 'The accused absconded after being granted bail, prompting the court to issue a non-bailable warrant.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Deterrence', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'The theory that punishment should be severe enough to discourage potential offenders from committing crimes.', usage: 'The court imposed a deterrent sentence to send a clear message against drunk driving.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Rehabilitation', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'The process of reforming an offender to prevent future criminal behaviour, emphasizing education and treatment.', usage: 'The juvenile was sent to a special home for rehabilitation rather than imprisonment.', section: 'Juvenile Justice Act, 2015'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Recidivism', category: 'Criminal', meaning: 'The tendency of a convicted criminal to reoffend after serving their punishment.', usage: 'The court noted the accused\'s high rate of recidivism — three convictions in five years — and denied bail.'),
  LegalTerm(term: 'Garnishment', category: 'Legal English', meaning: 'A legal process for collecting a debt by directing a third party holding funds of the debtor to pay the creditor.', usage: 'The court ordered garnishment of the judgment debtor\'s salary to recover the decretal amount in monthly installments.'),
];
